{
  "label": "Ask-side share of the premium the vendor sided",
  "definition": "share = sum(ask) / (sum(ask) + sum(bid)) over the windows that state askPrem, bidPrem and a positive prem, with neither side negative, where a window whose two sides sum past its premium is scaled by prem / (askPrem + bidPrem) before it is pooled; classified = sum over those windows of those scaled dollars (at most the window premium) / sum(prem) over every window with a positive prem, so premium on a window that states no side counts against the coverage and never as sided",
  "sides": {
    "ask": "classified >= 0.5 and share >= 0.65, both read as the whole percents printed",
    "bid": "classified >= 0.5 and share <= 0.35, both read as the whole percents printed",
    "mixed": "classified >= 0.5 and 0.35 < share < 0.65, read as the whole percents printed",
    "thin": "classified < 0.5 read as a whole percent (under 50% sided), including classified 0, where nothing was sided and there is no share",
    "null": "no usable window: classified is null, so the side was never stated"
  },
  "rounding": "the thresholds compare the whole percents the said form prints (+(v * 100).toFixed(0), half up), at 65, 35 and 50, so a figure is never printed once coloured and once plain; this departs from the literal thresholds of C-02 (share >= 0.65 or <= 0.35, classified >= 0.5) on three known answers (share 0.6496 is ask, share 0.3504 is bid, classified 0.4996 is coloured), and a server helper reproducing this table must round the same way",
  "said": "the share and classified as whole percents: \"<share>% ask side · <classified>% sided\"; \"none sided\" when classified is 0; an em dash when no window is usable",
  "split": "askSplit(row) for one window with a positive premium: { ask, bid, none, askStated, bidStated }; a side is stated when it is a number and not negative, and an unstated side is 0 dollars, so its share of the premium goes to none while the stated side keeps its dollars; sides summing past the premium are scaled by prem / (ask + bid); when both are stated, ask / (ask + bid) is share and (ask + bid) / prem is classified",
  "tolerance": 1e-12,
